ry":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Affected: v4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f], v4.7.rc1.official [a4f5e8cdd], v4.7.dev1.official [bf95b6258]\n- Unaffected: v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4], v4.6.stable.official [89cea1439], v4.6.rc2.official [78c6632eb], v4.6.rc1.official [481f36ed2]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.7) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M2 - Apple M2 (8 threads) - 8.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nZooming in on the outline of a label with a large font size causes the outline to grow while the \"Auto Resample CanvasItems\" setting is enabled, on any renderer.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a Label node and input some text\n- Set its font size to 256 and its outline size to 16\n- Set its outline color to black\n- Ensure the \"Auto Resample CanvasItems\" setting in the View menu is enabled\n- Zoom in on the edge of the outline in the viewport\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[OutlineRepro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29411612/OutlineRepro.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120689/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}